Package: stanliWebR
Title: Sample brms and rbmi Models with stanli in WebAssembly
Version: 0.7.0
Authors@R: c(person("Lukas", "Widmer", email = "lukas_andreas.widmer@novartis.com",
                    role = c("aut", "cre")),
             person("Novartis", "Pharma AG", role = "cph"))
Author: Lukas Widmer [aut, cre],
  Novartis Pharma AG [cph]
Maintainer: Lukas Widmer <lukas_andreas.widmer@novartis.com>
Description: brms and rbmi both hand a Stan program to rstan, which compiles it
    with a C++ toolchain and so cannot work in WebAssembly. This package swaps the
    few package internals that compile and sample for equivalents that run the same
    program through stanli, a Stan interpreter, and hand back an ordinary rstan
    'stanfit'. Everything downstream -- summaries, posterior predictions, loo, rbmi's
    diagnostics and draw extraction -- is the packages' own code. RBesT and
    OncoBayes2, which sample precompiled models with rstan::sampling(), are routed
    to stanli the same way, and so does rstan's own stan_model() and sampling().
    Loading the package arranges for each of them to be
    patched whenever it is loaded, so brm() with its default backend,
    rbmi::method_bayes(), RBesT::gMAP(), OncoBayes2::blrm_exnex() and
    rstan::stan_model() work unchanged. These packages, rstan and stanli are listed under Suggests only so
    that the package installs outside WebAssembly; the patches report what they
    could not find.
